-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Real</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Feinstein</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bjornstad</surname><given-names>ON</given-names></name><name><surname>Krebs</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Predicting the local dynamics of epizootic rabies among raccoons in the United States</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2000</year><volume>97</volume><fpage>13666</fpage><lpage>13671</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11069300</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.240326697</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hanlon</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Willsey</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Laniewicz</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Trimarchi</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Rupprecht</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>New York State oral wildlife vaccination: first evaluation for enzootic racoon rabies control</article-title><source>Conference Program and Abstracts of the 7th Annual Rabies in the Americas: 9&#x02013;13 December 1996, Atlanta, Georgia, USA</source></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hanlon</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Childs</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Nettles</surname><given-names>VF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Recommendations of a national working group on prevention and control of rabies in the United States. Article III: Rabies in wildlife</article-title><source>J Am Vet Med Assoc</source><year>1999</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>1612</fpage><lpage>1619</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1457502