0.1016/j.vaccine.2005.07.041</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gosselin</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>Lebel</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Rivest</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Fradet</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Integrated System for Public Health Monitoring of West Nile Virus (ISPHM-WNV): a real-time GIS for surveillance and decision-making</article-title><source>Int JHealth Geogr</source><year>2005</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>21</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16159403</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1476-072X-4-21</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name><name><surname>Eidson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmit</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ellis</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kulldorff</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Geographic prediction of human onset of West Nile virus using dead crow clusters: an evaluation of year 2002 data in New York State</article-title><source>Am J Epidemiol</source><year>2006</year><volume>163</volume><fpage>171</fpage><lpage>80</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16306307</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/aje/kwj023</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dwass</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modified randomization tests for nonparametric hypotheses</article-title><source>Annals of Mathematical Statistics</source><year>1957</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>181</fpage><lpage>187</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kulldorff</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><collab>Information Management Services, Inc</collab></person-group><article-title>SaTScan&#x02122; v5.1.3: Software for the spatial and space-time scan statistics</article-title><year>2005</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.satscan.org/"/></citation></ref><ref id="B32"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>SAS Institute Inc</collab></person-group><source>SAS 913 Help and Documentation</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Cary, NC: SAS Institute Inc</publisher-name></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>